From: Nick Schuetz <nschuetz@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Demote clang 21+ -Werror promotions back to warnings

Fedora 44 ships clang 19/20+ on stable and clang 22 in updates; clang 21
promoted -Wdeprecated-volatile and -Wcharacter-conversion to errors.
O3DE upstream's -Werror prevents the build from completing under these
compilers. Anchor on the -Werror line itself (stable across upstream
releases) and append two -Wno-error=... flags.

---
--- a/cmake/Platform/Common/Clang/Configurations_clang.cmake	2026-04-29 16:57:49.527909425 -0500
+++ b/cmake/Platform/Common/Clang/Configurations_clang.cmake	2026-04-29 16:58:01.375650022 -0500
@@ -64,6 +64,10 @@
         -fvisibility-inlines-hidden
         -Wall
         -Werror
+        # Fedora RPM build: clang 21+ promoted these to errors; demote
+        # back to warnings so upstream -Werror doesn't fail the build.
+        -Wno-error=deprecated-volatile
+        -Wno-error=character-conversion
 
         ###################
         # Disabled warnings (please do not disable any others without first consulting sig-build)
